{"book":19,"chapter":132,"context":{"chapter":132,"title":"Arise into Your Resting Place","summary":"The people remember David's vow to find a home for the ark, celebrate its arrival in Zion, and recall God's oath to keep David's sons on the throne and to dwell in Zion forever.","background":"Title: 'A Song of degrees.' A royal and Zion psalm, the longest Song of Ascents. Verse 6 recalls finding the ark 'in the fields of the wood,' likely Kirjath-jearim ('town of woods'), where it stayed for years (1 Samuel 7:1-2). Solomon's dedication prayer ends with verses 8–10 (2 Chronicles 6:41-42).","customs":[{"term":"A lamp for mine anointed","verses":"132:17","note":"A burning lamp pictured a family line that continues; God promised David a lasting lamp (1 Kings 11:36)."}],"watchFor":["David's oath (vv. 2–5) answered by God's oath (vv. 11–12).","Each request in verses 8–10 is answered in verses 14–18."],"connections":["2 Samuel 6:12-17","1 Samuel 7:1-2","2 Chronicles 6:41-42","2 Samuel 7:12-16"]},"verses":{"0":{"w":[["שִׁיר","shir","H7892","HNcmsc","[the] song of"],["הַמַּעֲלוֹת","hama'alot","H4609","HTd/Ncfpa","the ascents"]]},"1":{"w":[["זְכוֹר","zekhor-","H2142","HVqv2ms","remember"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","O Yahweh"],["לְדָוִד","ledavid","H1732","HR/Npm","to David"],["אֵת","'et","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["כָּל","kol-","H3605","HNcmsc","all"],["עֻנּוֹתוֹ","unoto","H6031","HVPcc/Sp3ms","being afflicted he"]],"x":[[19120001,19120001,7],[19129001,19129001,6],[19121001,19121001,5],[19126001,19126001,5],[25005001,25005001,5],[1008001,1008001,4],[2002024,2002024,4],[19125001,19125001,4],[19128001,19128001,4],[25003019,25003019,4]],"xn":14},"2":{"w":[["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","who"],["נִשְׁבַּע","nishba'","H7650","HVNp3ms","he swore an oath"],["לַיהוָה","layahweh","H3068","HR/Npt","to Yahweh"],["נָדַר","nadar","H5087","HVqp3ms","he vowed"],["לַאֲבִיר","la'avir","H46","HR/Aamsc","to [the] mighty one of"],["יַעֲקֹב","ya'ako","H3290","HNpm","Jacob"]],"x":[[1049024,1